          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best mower for a large yard is the one matched to the grass you actually mow, your terrain and what else you need it to do. For one to three flat acres with obstacles, the Toro TimeCutter 50 MyRIDE is our pick; with slopes or towing, the John Deere X380 is the steadier choice.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For three to four acres, step up to the Cub Cadet XT2 GX54 garden tractor or the EGO Z6 52 if you want battery power. And if your large yard is closer to half an acre to an acre, the Toro TimeMaster 30 walk-behind will do the job for a fraction of the cost of a rider.
